/*
====================================================================
In this application scenario, opening a breaker between
Buses 3 and 4 isolates the loads, the PV system, and the BESS
from the grid, effectively creating a microgrid configuration. In
this setup, the BESS operates in grid-forming mode, providing
voltage and frequency references for the microgrid. In contrast,
the PV system operates in grid-following mode, injecting
power based on available solar generation. During the islanded
condition, the system can be energized with the BESS and PV
as primary power sources.
====================================================================

Davis Montenegro and Robert Kerestes

2024

*/


! Comment out the line below if running from OpenDSS-G 
!Compile master.dss

! Forces the PV to deliver power only until reaching the 95% of the nominal voltage at its terminals  
pvsystem.pv1.safevoltage=0.9
solve

! Opens the switch between buses n3 and n4 
open line.line2 terminal=1
solve

! Sets the BESS to operate in GFM mode
edit storage.mystorage State = Discharging ControlMode = GFM  SafeVoltage=0

set mode=dynamics maxiterations=50 number=200 time=(10,0)
set loadshapeclass=daily

solve


! Use the plot routines below to plot the monitors using DSSView from stand alone DSS 
/*

! Export monitors
export monitors all

! active power output
plot monitor object=myPVPQ channels=(1,3, 5)
! Voltages at the PV Point of connection
plot monitor object=myPVVolt channels=(1,3, 5)
! Currents at the PV Point of connection
plot monitor object=myPVVolt channels=(7,9, 11)
*/